Build the two music devices (hw/audio/opl3.c and hw/audio/mpu401.c,
overlaid from libsynth/qemu/ by scripts/prepare-qemu.sh) when
-Dlibsynth_dir names the directory holding liblibsynth.a, the Rust
staticlib of the FM / General MIDI / CM-32L engines (libsynth/, built by
scripts/configure-qemu.sh). The same arrangement patch 50 uses for
libdisc, and for the same reason: the engines are ours, the wiring is
the patch. Doc 20 §1 and §5.

QEMU has no MPU-401 at all, and its sb16 carries no OPL — so before
this, a guest's *music* had nowhere to go, whatever its sound card.

diff --git a/hw/audio/meson.build b/hw/audio/meson.build
index 2154cbdb57..3c5f6a93d2 100644
--- a/hw/audio/meson.build
+++ b/hw/audio/meson.build
@@ -11,6 +11,11 @@ system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_MARVELL_88W8618', if_true: files('marvell_88w8618.c'
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_PCSPK', if_true: files('pcspk.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_PL041', if_true: files('pl041.c', 'lm4549.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_SB16', if_true: files('sb16.c'))
+# win98-xp-virt: the music devices — an OPL3 with the timers a detection
+# routine reads, and the MPU-401 QEMU has never had — over libsynth's
+# engines. Both files are overlaid by scripts/prepare-qemu.sh, and they
+# are built exactly when that staticlib was given (doc 20 §5).
+system_ss.add(when: libsynth, if_true: files('opl3.c', 'mpu401.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_VT82C686', if_true: files('via-ac97.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_WM8750', if_true: files('wm8750.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: ['CONFIG_VIRTIO_SND', 'CONFIG_VIRTIO'], if_true: files('virtio-snd.c'))
diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 72917ee927..17bae9d379 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -2026,6 +2026,25 @@ if get_option('libdisc_dir') != ''
                                link_args: libdisc_libs)
 endif
 
+# win98-xp-virt: libsynth, the music engines (a Rust staticlib built by
+# scripts/configure-qemu.sh) behind hw/audio/opl3.c and hw/audio/mpu401.c;
+# doc 20 §1. Same arrangement as libdisc above, and the same per-platform
+# link libraries, because it is the same Rust runtime underneath.
+libsynth = not_found
+if get_option('libsynth_dir') != ''
+  libsynth_lib = cc.find_library('libsynth', dirs: [get_option('libsynth_dir')],
+                                 static: true, required: true)
+  if host_os == 'darwin'
+    libsynth_libs = ['-liconv']
+  elif host_os == 'windows'
+    libsynth_libs = ['-lkernel32', '-lntdll', '-luserenv', '-lws2_32', '-ldbghelp']
+  else
+    libsynth_libs = ['-ldl', '-lm', '-lrt', '-lutil', '-lgcc_s']
+  endif
+  libsynth = declare_dependency(dependencies: [libsynth_lib, threads],
+                                link_args: libsynth_libs)
+endif
+
 lzo = not_found
 if not get_option('lzo').auto() or have_system
   lzo = cc.find_library('lzo2', has_headers: ['lzo/lzo1x.h'],
@@ -2465,6 +2484,7 @@ config_host_data.set('CONFIG_POSIX', host_os != 'windows')
 config_host_data.set('CONFIG_WIN32', host_os == 'windows')
 config_host_data.set('CONFIG_LZO', lzo.found())
 config_host_data.set('CONFIG_CDIMAGE', libdisc.found())
+config_host_data.set('CONFIG_LIBSYNTH', libsynth.found())
 config_host_data.set('CONFIG_MPATH', mpathpersist.found())
 config_host_data.set('CONFIG_BLKIO', blkio.found())
 if blkio.found()
@@ -5055,6 +5075,7 @@ summary_info += {'IGVM support':      igvm}
 summary_info += {'libssh support':    libssh}
 summary_info += {'lzo support':       lzo}
 summary_info += {'cdimage (libdisc)':  libdisc}
+summary_info += {'music (libsynth)':   libsynth}
 summary_info += {'snappy support':    snappy}
 summary_info += {'bzip2 support':     libbzip2}
 summary_info += {'lzfse support':     liblzfse}
